From d5e54b1a3360ae295928444aee7c7ff7d401c466 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TribalEarth AI Dev <dev@tribalearth.local>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 14:39:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add multilingual voice-assisted claim filing + fix
 placeholder localization bug
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Fixed root cause of untranslated placeholders: data-i18n-placeholder
  attributes referenced keys (form.step1.applicantPlaceholder, etc.)
  that didn't exist in any locale file. Added all 11 missing keys
  across all 6 languages (en, hi, bn, or, te, sat), reusing existing
  bilingual dictionary names/places for consistency.
- Fixed 4 real script-mixing bugs found while cross-checking
  bilingual.js: stray Devanagari/Telugu/Khmer/Gurmukhi characters
  accidentally embedded in Odia and Santali text.
- Extended i18n config.js to also localize title/aria-label attributes
  (data-i18n-title, data-i18n-aria-label).
- Added voice namespace (142 keys total now, full parity across all
  6 languages) covering mic labels, voice states, and the guided
  voice-fill flow.
- New backend: services/bhashiniService.js (honest Bhashini API
  abstraction — never fakes a result without real credentials),
  services/extractionService.js (rule-based structured field
  extraction, tested against spec examples), .env.example.
- New routes: POST /api/voice/transcribe, /api/voice/extract,
  POST /api/voice/tts. All honestly return 503 'not configured'
  without Bhashini credentials rather than faking success.
- New frontend: public/js/voice.js — per-field mic buttons (browser
  Web Speech API for en/hi/bn/te, honestly flagged unsupported for
  or/sat pending Bhashini), guided 'Fill Using Voice' sequential flow
  with safe review-before-autofill (Current vs Detected, never
  silent overwrite), two-tier TTS (Bhashini first, browser fallback).
- Existing multilingual/bilingual architecture, Steps 2/3 core
  behavior, claims register, search/filters, audit trail, and all
  existing API routes left untouched and verified working.
